OL,3,APassports needed for ferry passengers
OL,4,Atravelling between UK and Ireland
OL,5,
OL,6,FPassengers travelling on ferries
OL,7,Fbetween the UK and Ireland will need to
OL,8,Fshow their passport from Monday.
OL,10,FFerry operator Irish Ferries said the
OL,11,Fnew requirement applies to their Dublin
OL,12,Fto Holyhead and Rosslare to Pembroke
OL,13,Froutes, in both directions.
OL,15,FStena Line said all passengers
OL,16,Ftravelling from Dublin, Holyhead,
OL,17,FFishguard or Rosslare ports would also
OL,18,Fbe required to present a valid passport
OL,19,Fat check-in.
OL,23,APub: 28-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
